<title>MEXICO: Mexico international steel forum slated Oct 10-11.</title>
<headline>Mexico international steel forum slated Oct 10-11.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guadalajara is to host an international steelmakers' forum on October 10 and 11, and speakers have been invited from Mexican, U.S. and Canadian steel firms, organisers said on Monday.</p>
<p>The forum, &quot;Mexico on the Mend - Steel Comes off the Floor,&quot; will be run under the auspices of the magazine American Metal Market and focus on steel markets in Mexico and industry forecasts for 1996 and 1997.</p>
<p>Invited panelists include Mario Concha of  G.S. Industries Inc and Luis Garcia Limon, CEO at Grupo Simec.</p>
<p>Guadalajara is Mexico's second city and capital of the western state of Jalisco, a major steelmaking center.</p>
<p>-- Guadalajara newsroom 523 817-0397</p>
</text>
